  \[
  \mathrm{LeftHomotopyClass}(X,Y)\simeq \mathrm{RightHomotopyClass}(X,Y).
  \]
  This equivalence preserves the underlying localized morphism, so the two comparison maps have equivalent bijectivity. This is exactly `bijective_leftHomotopyClassToHom_iff_bijective_rightHomotopyClassToHom`.

- The fundamental lemma then states that the left comparison map is bijective; use `bijective_leftHomotopyClassToHom` for the second conjunct.

